  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S2 was converted from a pass/fail gate into a review trigger at 5% with no sales stop and no numeric permanent limit, which protects Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%); per-model results go to regulators and purchasers but not the public. S5 kept an automatic mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition, which captures Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9), while S3 gives six years for retrofitting installed units (favouring Northwind's 38% coverage) and S4 sets built-in suppression at 36 months (favouring Halcyon's cost position)."
